(P/'REPORT.md').write_text('Bounded DHCP TX review — installed ee8b6da0\n\nThe unique PID evidence now identifies real firmware MPDU_ERROR for every sampled ordinary frame. Initial capture:43 ordinary failures including10 DISCOVERs. Later capture:63 ordinary failures including27 DISCOVERs; management and M2/M4 succeed, and critically protected G2 PID34 also succeeds at rate0/count1. This rules out treating protection, rate0, or a universally missing PTK as the established cause.\n\nAll ordinary observed traffic is Ethernet group/broadcast; the successful EAPOL packets are unicast to the AP. This is the strongest remaining comparison axis, not a demonstrated bug. Android infrastructure routing still correctly sends group Ethernet via the AP peer/PTK. Native follows it; changing DHCP to GTK/BMC/noACK would contradict selected source.\n\nProtectedG2 and DHCP use the same HW0/TXP path and descriptor controls after nstx_build normalizes VTA, fixed-rate and NO_AGG. Length/PID/token and Ethernet payload differ. STA BMC255 and pairwise CMD7 fields match the selected source. No additional source-proven field correction is established.\n\nPriority: compare actual ordinary unicast versus group data using genuine network observations and unique PID; if group-specific, inspect private over-air ToDS/converted header and AP ACK/decryption counters. A firmware WTBL dump is not casually read-only: selected debug code writes its selector. No arbitrary descriptor/key/rate write or network-success claim is justified. Full pins, exact source anchors, counts and limits are in report.json.\n\nNo hardware command, source edit, build, CI or gate action.\n')
